Q: Plink fails to run when executed from PHP in wamp, but works when executed manually A: <p>Do not launch external tool for SSH.</p>
<p>PHP has <a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/book.ssh2.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">native support for SSH</a>.</p>
<p>Or use <a href="https://phpseclib.sourceforge.net/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">phpseclib</a>:</p>
<pre><code>require __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';

use phpseclib\Net\SSH2;

$ssh = new SSH2($hostname);
if ($ssh-&gt;login($username, $password))
{
    echo $ssh-&gt;exec(&quot;df -h&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
<p>See:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://phpseclib.com/docs/ssh2/connect" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://phpseclib.com/docs/ssh2/connect</a></li>
<li><a href="https://phpseclib.com/docs/ssh2/auth" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://phpseclib.com/docs/ssh2/auth</a></li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p>Anyway, if you want to use Plink, redirect also the standard error output to debug your problem:</p>
<pre><code>plink.exe .. dir &gt; 11.txt 2&gt;&amp;1
</code></pre>
<p>See <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/q/1420965/850848">How can I redirect Windows cmd standard output and standard error to a single file?</a>.</p>
<p>You are for sure missing the <a href="https://the.earth.li/%7Esgtatham/putty/latest/htmldoc/Chapter3.html#using-cmdline-hostkey" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>-hostkey</code> switch</a> to explicitly specify a fingerprint of the trusted hostkey.</p>
